      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Complications after endometrial ablation are uncommon, and published series show that the majority of women who are treated by this technique remain symptom free in the postoperative period. A 39-year-old woman with previous tubal ligation underwent laparoscopic-assisted vaginal hysterectomy for debilitating pelvic pain 1 year after endometrial ablation. Pathologic assessment of the surgical specimen showed bilateral hematosalpinges from continued cyclic occult bleeding. The symptoms and findings in this case confirm the postablation-tubal sterilization syndrome."},
